{"title":"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The singers in Saura’s choir have heights\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/d/dadc74bb507a8c64acabe09fed091d462ff7a644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$148 \\text{ cm}, 141 \\text{ cm}, 172.5 \\text{ cm}, 168 \\text{ cm}, 151.5 \\text{ cm}, 183.5 \\text{ cm}, 178.5 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"485\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<p>What is the range of their heights?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c4971fa2a6cc8be4cac576b0b3578cc80d4acddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 42.5 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 27 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 52.5 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 37.5 \\text{ cm} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 31.5 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"587\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Range\" title=\"Range\">range</a> of a dataset is equal to the largest number in the dataset minus the smallest number in the dataset. \n</p><p>We can see that the largest height of the choir is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e955bd8ec76dc72c2bd61430f33682ab9cb7485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$183.5 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> and the smallest height of the choir is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250c77c6f84684379450929f22fa21ea2e7a7bae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />. The range of their heights would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/90911a6b8296f1a7227317a82da47825a907da1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$183.5 \\text{ cm} - 141 \\text{ cm} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 42.5 \\text{ cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"277\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</